  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-38" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-39" contextRef="c-1">Q2</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-40" contextRef="c-1">Florida Southeast Connection, LLC</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-41" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-42" contextRef="c-1">Q2</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-43" contextRef="c-1">Florida Southeast Connection, LLC</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-44" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-45" contextRef="c-1">Q2</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-46" contextRef="c-1">Florida Southeast Connection, LLC</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:ReportYear id="f-47" contextRef="c-1" decimals="0" unitRef="u-1">2026</ferc:ReportYear>
  <ferc:ReportPeriod id="f-48" contextRef="c-1">Q2</ferc:ReportPeriod>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-49" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Introduction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP"). These requirements differ from GAAP related to (1) the presentation of income taxes (2) the presentation of unamortized debt expense, (3) the presentation of regulatory debits and credits and (4) the presentation of regulatory assets and liabilities. The Notes to the Financial Statements have been prepared in conformity with GAAP. Accordingly, certain footnotes are not prepared on the same basis as the financial statements presented herein.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements should be read in conjunction with the 2025 FERC Form 2 of Florida Southeast Connection, LLC ("FSC" or the "Company"). In the opinion of FSC's management, all adjustments considered necessary for fair financial statement presentation have been made. The results of operations for an interim period generally will not give a true indication of results for the year. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:123%"&gt;FLORIDA SOUTHEAST CONNECTION, LLC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:123%"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:104%"&gt;For the periods ended June 30, 2026 and 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:104%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;1. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt; OPERATING REVENUES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;All of the Company&#8217;s operating revenues for the periods ended June 30, 2026 and 2025 represent revenue from contracts with customers for natural gas transportation services. For the three months ended June 30, 2026, and 2025, FSC's operating revenues from its contract with FPL were approximatel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt; $23 million and $23.6 million&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;, respectively. As an open access pipeline regulated by FERC, FSC must make available any unsubscribed or operationally available capacity to shippers that are qualified to take service under its tariff and agree to pay the rates in the FERC Gas Tariff.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;The Company's accounts receivable and accounts receivable from associated companies are related to revenues earned from contracts with customers. Receivables represent unconditional rights to consideration and reflect the differences in timing of revenue recognition and cash collections. For substantially all of the Company's receivables, customer and counterparty credit risk is managed in the same manner and the terms and conditions of payment are similar.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;The Company recognizes revenues as natural gas transportation services are performed, consistent with the amounts billed to customers. The Company considers the amount billed to represent the value of services provided to the customer. The Company&#8217;s customers typically receive bills monthly with payment due within 30 days. The contracts with customers related to pipeline service revenues contain a fixed price related to firm natural gas transportation capacity with maturity dates in 2042, 2044 and 2045. At June 30, 2026, the Company expects to record approximately &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;$1.2 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;billion of revenue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;s over the remaining terms of the related contracts as the capacity is provided.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;2. RELATED-PARTY TRANSACTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;As discussed in Note 1, FSC&#8217;s revenue is primarily derived from the Transportation Services Agreement ("TSA") with FPL. FSC also has transportation imbalances arise from their TSA with FPL at the point where the FSC pipeline connects with FPL's fuel infrastructure (referred to as Martin Location). From time to time, dekatherms of natural gas confirmed and scheduled to be delivered to or received from the Martin Location may be greater or less than the dekatherms of gas which are actually delivered, thus creating an imbalance. These imbalances are &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;reflected in either accounts payable to associated companies or accounts receivable from associated companies on the comparative balance sheets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;FSC has an administrative services agreement ("ASA") with NextEra Energy Resources, LLC ("NEER"), an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of NEE, and an operation and maintenance ("O&amp;amp;M") agreement with NextEra Energy Pipeline Services, LLC ("NEPSCO") whereby the Company pays a fee equal to the sum of all actual direct and indirect costs and expenses for services performed under the agreements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%"&gt;As part of a credit support arrangement provided in FSC's third party Note Purchase Agreement, NEE and its subsidiaries may withdraw funds held by the Company in exchange for qualifying credit support provided to the Company's lenders. NEE and its subsidiaries may keep the funds until the Company makes a permitted distribution under the financing arrangement, requires funds to pay debt service or expenses of the Company, or otherwise if the Company demands the return of such funds. If NEE or its subsidiaries fail to return withdrawn funds when required by the Company's Note Purchase Agreement, the lenders will be entitled to draw on credit support provided by NEE in the amount of such withdrawn funds. If NEE or one of its affiliates realizes any earnings on the withdrawn funds prior to the return of such funds, it will be permitted to retain those earnings. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:118%"&gt;3. SUBSEQUENT EVENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Management has evaluated the impact of events occurring after June 30, 2026, up to August&#160;21, 2026. These financial statements include all necessary adjustments and disclosures resulting from such evaluation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;*******&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
